    <!-- Column 2 Text -->
    <div slot="col-2-text">
      <p>
        When purple heather clothes the hills <br />
        They are an awe inspiring sight <br />
        That keeps bringing back the exiles <br />
        Filling hearts of tourists with delight.
      </p>

      <p>
        This month of colourful glory comes <br />
        Before the Scottish summer’s end; <br />
        Bringing a hint of autumn too <br />
        As Harvesters homeward wend.
      </p>

      <p>
        In the orchards, fruit is ripening <br />
        Swallows are ready for the flight; <br />
        Daylight hours are growing shorter <br />
        And hoards of midges start to bite.
      </p>

      <p>
        Fresh vegetables are still plentiful <br />
        Growing for use in soups and stews; <br />
        Peas, beans, carrots and courgettes <br />
        Are still growing for us to use.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Column 3 Middle Images -->
    <div slot="col-3-images">
      <img
        src="/poems/august-poem-the-heather-hills-of-august/image-2.avif"
        alt=""
      />
      <img
        src="/poems/august-poem-the-heather-hills-of-august/image-3.avif"
        alt=""
