      <img
        src="/poems/august-poem-the-heather-hills-of-august/image-5.avif"
        alt=""
      />
    </div>

    <!-- Column 4 Text -->
    <div slot="col-4-text">
      <p>
        Flowers in tubs and borders <br />
        All standing stately and tall; <br />
        While giving a colourful showing <br />
        Can’t compete with one quite small.
      </p>

      <p>
        This little native plant of ours <br />
        That keeps growing wild and free; <br />
        Still bringing folk here from afar <br />
        It’s wondrous beauty for to see.
      </p>

      <p>
        Each month has a special something <br />
        That is quite different from the rest; <br />
        And miles of heather in full bloom <br />
        Now see’s August at its best.
      </p>
    </div>

